Global Pullulan market was valued at USD 71 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 112 million by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 5.2 % during the forecast period (2026–2034). This growth is propelled by the rapid rise of clean‑label food solutions, expanding regulatory mandates for biodegradable packaging, and breakthrough advances in AI‑assisted fermentation that are lowering production costs and improving purity.

Pullulan is an extracellular, water‑soluble polysaccharide produced by fermentation of the black yeast Aureobasidium pullulans. First isolated in the late‑1930s, it combines non‑toxicity with strong film‑forming, adhesive and oxygen‑barrier properties, making it suitable for edible food coatings, rapid‑dissolve pharmaceutical capsules and fully compostable packaging solutions.

